{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1408724-can-a-demon-give-the-souls-from-their-soul-pacts-to-changelings","id":1408724,"title":"Can a Demon give the Souls from their Soul Pacts to Changelings?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-17T08:38:57-07:00","id":1408724,"title":"Can a Demon give the Souls from their Soul Pacts to Changelings?","content":"Listened to an actual play podcast where they mentioned Icons being parts of a human soul. Made me wonder if a Demon making a Soul Pact might give the leftover Soul to a Changeling to create Icons. Granted there isn't a person who can reclaim this Icon. Maybe a bartering chip for Goblin Markets.<br /> <br /> Yeah its probably too harsh for a &quot;nice&quot; Changeling to agree to. But man it seems interesting.<br /> <br /> Additionally I could definitely see Souls from Soul Pacts turning into Hedge Ghost like entities in the Hedge. Since Demons don't really know where the Souls from a Soul Pact go after its been cashed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T08:45:48-07:00","id":1408726,"title":"","content":"Unless I'm forgetting something, Soul Pacts dont actually take souls. It &quot;only&quot; takes that person's existence away from him so the demon can take his place. Other than that, the soul is gone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T09:43:27-07:00","id":1408735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1408724-can-a-demon-give-the-souls-from-their-soul-pacts-to-changelings?p=1408726#post1408726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless I'm forgetting something, Soul Pacts dont actually take souls. It &quot;only&quot; takes that person's existence away from him so the demon can take his place. Other than that, the soul is gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>The DTD rule book calls out that the Demon doesn't exactly know where the Soul goes. And based on the Echo creatures that get created from Burned Covers it seems that the Soul exists somewhere.<br /> <br /> Echoes are the remnants of the Cover's Soul that manifests after a Cover gets destroyed. They usually behave like ghosts, with the added mission of taking over the life of the Demon that burned them.<br /> <br /> There is a lot left up to interpretation as to where the Soul goes as most Demons don't care and while its not explicitly stated it is assumed that like all Pacts if a Soul Pact is destroyed the Soul and Body of the person who sold their soul is returned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T11:31:32-07:00","id":1408754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1408724-can-a-demon-give-the-souls-from-their-soul-pacts-to-changelings?p=1408735#post1408735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The DTD rule book calls out that the Demon doesn't exactly know where the Soul goes. And based on the Echo creatures that get created from Burned Covers it seems that the Soul exists somewhere.<br /> <br /> Echoes are the remnants of the Cover's Soul that manifests after a Cover gets destroyed. They usually behave like ghosts, with the added mission of taking over the life of the Demon that burned them.<br /> <br /> There is a lot left up to interpretation as to where the Soul goes as most Demons don't care and while its not explicitly stated it is assumed that like all Pacts if a Soul Pact is destroyed the Soul and Body of the person who sold their soul is returned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehh, whatever happens to the soul is still out of the Demon's control. If they cant even figure out where they go, how do are they expected to be able to trade with Changelings? As for Echoes, I'm pretty sure they are just a unique ghost. A metaphysical trauma like any other, just with a unique situation for it to have come into being","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T12:33:27-07:00","id":1408766,"title":"","content":"The short answer is &quot;No.&quot;<br /> <br /> Explaining why, Icons and pacts bearing bits of a person's existence aren't neccesarily different things-in fact, they are hella comparable, enough that it's clear why the perception for overlap is there-but changelings don't <i>make</i> Icons so much as Icons are formed <i>from</i> changelings (or rather, mid-abuduction changelings) as they are dragged through the Hedge and the thorns take their due. What's more is that changelings aren't ghosts or demons-they don't <i>just</i> benefit from anyone's Icons, but instead any given changeling must take in Icons that are <i>theirs</i> to receive benefits.<br /> <br /> The best takeaway for this sort of interaction is that a) a pact made with a person pre-Durance probably counts as an Icon for a changeling, and reclaiming it has all the benefits of reclaiming an Icon but with the caveat of it being taken away (Unless it can then be internalized somehow, which, considering Changeling, is not the hardest thing you could set out to do, even if it's not contra-wise easy), and b) in this way, pacts made with pre-Durance changelings that find their way into the fairy trade will be valued and traded in likewise values and purposes as any other icon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T16:12:30-07:00","id":1408804,"title":"","content":"Ya, a soul pact isn't actually the soul. A soul is destroyed when a demon claims the soul pact. While mant things can be sold at goblin markets I feel this would be something that could maybe be sold (transfer pacts) but I dont think the reciever could do anything with it unless they were a demon themself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T21:29:59-07:00","id":1408852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1408724-can-a-demon-give-the-souls-from-their-soul-pacts-to-changelings?p=1408766#post1408766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best takeaway for this sort of interaction is that a) a pact made with a person pre-Durance probably counts as an Icon for a changeling, and reclaiming it has all the benefits of reclaiming an Icon but with the caveat of it being taken away (Unless it can then be internalized somehow, which, considering Changeling, is not the hardest thing you could set out to do, even if it's not contra-wise easy), and b) in this way, pacts made with pre-Durance changelings that find their way into the fairy trade will be valued and traded in likewise values and purposes as any other icon.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would look something like the way the Empty integrate Tokens into themselves, sans lichdom and getting to keep your heart at the end. Which is to say, not that mechanically challenging given enough time, but uncovering all the rotes would be a pain in the ass.<br /> <br /> And just to take that one step further, if (BIG IF) you wanted mechanics for a Changeling trying to integrate someone else's pact instead of their own, you could probably model something based on the Empty, but up the Clarity damage and potentially let you integrate some of the cover instead. 100% non-canon, it's just me riffing off an idea, but it could be cool in the right game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T05:54:59-07:00","id":1408896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1408724-can-a-demon-give-the-souls-from-their-soul-pacts-to-changelings?p=1408852#post1408852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would look something like the way the Empty integrate Tokens into themselves, sans lichdom and getting to keep your heart at the end. Which is to say, not that mechanically challenging given enough time, but uncovering all the rotes would be a pain in the ass.<br /> <br /> And just to take that one step further, if (BIG IF) you wanted mechanics for a Changeling trying to integrate someone else's pact instead of their own, you could probably model something based on the Empty, but up the Clarity damage and potentially let you integrate some of the cover instead. 100% non-canon, it's just me riffing off an idea, but it could be cool in the right game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Down this route lies a Empty-Absent hybrid and that delights and terrifies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}